 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "rNBi21SFCAAJ",
   "from": "Karl Fetter",
   "author": "d097239898b13d0a",
   "date": "2018-04-12T14:49:35Z",
   "subject": "Confidence Intervals for poppr's other diversity statistics (e.g. Heterozygosity)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p><span><font size=\"4\">Hello, </font></span></p><p><span><font size=\"4\"><br></font></span></p><p><span><font size=\"4\">I’d like to calculate confidence intervals for the expected and observed heterozygosity and I’m not sure if it’s possible to do that within poppr’s tools. Is this possible? I’d like to have output similar to what the diversity_ci function does for exp. heterozygosity. Is it possible to expand the stats that diversity_ci will calculate beyond the four that currently exist?</font></span></p><p><span><font size=\"4\"><br></font></span></p><p><span><font size=\"4\">Thanks,</font></span></p><p><span><font size=\"4\"><br></font></span></p><p><span><font size=\"4\">Karl</font></span></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "w_6rBjpiCAAJ",
   "from": "Zhian Kamvar",
   "author": "d192ec4b1d416345",
   "date": "2018-04-12T16:15:41Z",
   "subject": "Re: [poppr] Confidence Intervals for poppr's other diversity statistics (e.g. Heterozygosity)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>Technically, expected and observed heterozygosity are calculated by adegenet (unless you are referring to the &quot;Hexp&quot; column in the poppr() function). </div><div><br></div><div>Unfortunately, diversity_ci() can only work for multilocus genotypes due to the differences between the type of data represented by multilocus genotype counts and alleles. However, you can roll-your-own with the shufflepop() function (assuming that you want to get an estimate of these values in a random-mating scenario). Here are the steps:</div><div><br></div><div>1. Generate 1000 simulations of your data from allele frequencies with shufflepop(method = 2)</div><div>2. Calculate expected and observed heterozygosity for each</div><div>3. Calculate the 5% and 95% quantiles.</div><div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s an example using data from a colony of cats in Nancy, France:</div><div><br></div><div><pre><code><font face=\"Noto Mono\"><span>suppressPackageStartupMessages(library</span>(<span>&quot;poppr&quot;</span>))\r\ndata(nancycats)\r\nnan9 &lt;- nancycats[pop = <span>9</span>]\r\nhet &lt;- <span>function</span>(i){x &lt;- summary(i);c(Hexp = mean(x$Hexp), Hobs = mean(x$Hobs))}\r\nnan9samples &lt;- replicate(<span>1000</span>, shufflepop(nan9, method = <span>2</span>))\r\nres &lt;- sapply(nan9samples, het)\r\napply(res, <span>1</span>, quantile, c(<span>0.05</span>, <span>0.95</span>))\r\n<span>#&gt;          Hexp      Hobs</span>\r\n<span>#&gt; 5%  0.5781893 0.5679012</span>\r\n<span>#&gt; 95% 0.6556927 0.7407407</span>\r\nhet(nan9) <span># observed</span>\r\n<span>#&gt;      Hexp      Hobs </span>\r\n<span>#&gt; 0.6556927 0.7407407</span></font></code></pre></div><div><br></div><div>Hope that helps,</div><div>Zhian</div><div><br></div><div><div>\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">-----</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Zhian N. Kamvar, Ph. D.</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Postdoctoral Researcher (Everhart Lab)</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Department of Plant Pathology</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">University of Nebraska-Lincoln</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">ORCID: 0000-0003-1458-7108</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br></div><br></div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
