     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><div style=\"margin:0px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\"><span><font size=\"4\">Hello, </font></span></div><div style=\"margin:0px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\"><span><font size=\"4\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"margin:0px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\"><span><font size=\"4\">I’d like to calculate confidence intervals for the expected and observed heterozygosity and I’m not sure if it’s possible to do that within poppr’s tools. Is this possible? I’d like to have output similar to what the diversity_ci function does for exp. heterozygosity. Is it possible to expand the stats that diversity_ci will calculate beyond the four that currently exist?</font></span></div><div style=\"margin:0px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\"><span><font size=\"4\"><br></font></span></div><div style=\"margin:0px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\"><span><font size=\"4\">Thanks,</font></span></div><div style=\"margin:0px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\"><span><font size=\"4\"><br></font><